colorburst: factory-install Crostini DLCs (termina, termina-tools, edk2-ovmf).

Add the three DLC IDs Crostini needs to chromite's factory-install allowlist so
their overlay-colorburst ebuilds (which set DLC_FACTORY_INSTALL=true) are
accepted. Without this, build_dlc dies with "DLC=<id> is not allowed to be
factory installed" at both ebuild build time (EbuildParams.VerifyDlcParameters)
and image build time (dlc_lib.IsFactoryInstallAllowed). Factory-installing bakes
each dlc.img into the release image's stateful unencrypted/dlc-factory-images/
area so dlcservice installs Crostini's termina VM from local storage, never
contacting the colorburst update server (which serves only the OS payload, not
DLCs). See overlay-colorburst/chromeos-base/{termina-dlc,termina-tools-dlc,
edk2-ovmf-dlc}.

--- a/lib/dlc_allowlist.py
+++ b/lib/dlc_allowlist.py
@@ -14,7 +14,21 @@
 
 # Add DLC ID that requires factory installation.
 # By default, factory installed DLCs are allowed to be powerwash safe.
-DLC_FACTORY_INSTALL = (r"sample-dlc",)
+#
+# colorburst: termina-dlc, termina-tools-dlc and edk2-ovmf-dlc are
+# factory-installed into the release image (their overlay-colorburst ebuilds set
+# DLC_FACTORY_INSTALL=true) so the "Linux development environment" (Crostini)
+# installs entirely from local storage. The colorburst update server serves only
+# the OS payload, not DLCs, so the upstream OTA delivery path for these DLCs can
+# never succeed on our fleet. This allowlist is enforced both at ebuild build
+# time (EbuildParams.VerifyDlcParameters) and at image build time
+# (dlc_lib.IsFactoryInstallAllowed), so all three IDs must be listed here.
+DLC_FACTORY_INSTALL = (
+    r"sample-dlc",
+    r"termina-dlc",
+    r"termina-tools-dlc",
+    r"edk2-ovmf-dlc",
+)
 
 # Add DLC ID that requires factory installation with regex matching.
 # By default, factory installed DLCs are allowed to be powerwash safe.
